    kfree(mr);
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the driver frees the Memory Region (MR) structure (`mr`) even when the deregistration process fails (indicated by a non-zero return code `rc`). This leads to a null pointer dereference when the system attempts to access the already freed structure during a retry of the deregistration.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (rc) {
    dev_err(rdev_to_dev(rdev), "Dereg MR failed: %#x\n", rc);
    return rc;
}
```
Reason:
The fix ensures that if the deregistration fails (i.e., `rc` is non-zero), the error is logged, and the function returns early without freeing the MR structure. This prevents the structure from being freed prematurely, thus avoiding the null pointer dereference during subsequent attempts to deregister the MR.

